  "_comment": [
    "Hand-authored coordinates for the ground this system actually works.",
    "",
    "Bangalore is the launch metro, so its neighbourhoods are the common case, and the",
    "common case should cost nothing: a seeded area resolves with no HTTP call, no",
    "geocoder quota, and no rate-limit wait. Nominatim exists for everywhere else.",
    "",
    "Coordinates are neighbourhood centres accurate to a few hundred metres, which is well",
    "inside the 3km sweep radius they are used with. `aliases` cover spellings that survive",
    "normalisation as different words -- normalisation already strips case, spaces and",
    "punctuation, so 'J.P. Nagar' needs no alias but 'Malleswaram' does.",
    "",
    "`cities` carry a 15km city-wide centre, used when an operator names no areas."
  ],
